      "author": {
        "_id": "59b80cbbd1662e660835c7c5",
        "alias": "Neat Swordtail",
        "aliasID": "65ba016fed6eefce4cf1884a",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/c959bcb3ee68106f8a04726004a45aa2.jpg",
        "created": "2017-09-12T16:35:07.113Z",
        "name": "Noe",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2018-11-07T00:40:27.980Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "5be2347bad1fcc141b9e4d8f",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I'm mildly surprised, however not shocked due to how busy the dev team are with improving the featureset of VRChat that after more than a year of being on Steam this app hasn't really seen any hardware utilisation optimisations to try to improve the performance, especially in VR. \n\nWhile running Unity 2018 with multi-threading would be a good start, I don't feel this is the entire solution as I have a 4 core CPU (i7 4820K) and VRChat does hammer all 4 cores when I'm in a heavily packed world. Maybe it would start utilising my Hyperthreads but that wouldn't really provide much more than about a 5-10% improvement since hyperthreads are just additional instruction pipelines that keep the cores busier.\n\nWhat's definitely needed is code optimisations for IK frame processing and general hardware utilisation. Especially when you compare VRChat's performance to, say SurrealVR, where you can maintain a far higher framerate in a busy worlds and with fairly low hardware usage compared to VRChat, which absolutely LOVES to fill VRAM and load the CPU while barely touching the GPU.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Improve VRChat's performance!!",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "5b3ffb3c8541221eece59d4d",
      "private": false,
      "spam": false,
      "synthetic": true,
      "value": ""
    },
