      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ac4fd763f8d523278a414f7|full_name}: That depends on how the devs are able to build on the newer unity version, as while the engine itself might be multi-threaded, it still needs to be given instructions on how to efficiently manage the extra cores and/or threads. Especially on AMD \"Zen\" based CPUs which by design have giant latency differentials between sets of cores in different logic units (also known as CCX units) which is the hard part that will take time to improve after the jump to Unity 2018.x. Even Microsoft haven't optimised Windows' task scheduler to be able to efficiently handle these chips for optimum performance yet!",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-07-06T23:29:00.225Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRC's performance with multiple people in the room always hasn't been the best. \nI wish that the VRC Team would focus more on optimizing the games performance.\n\nSadly I'm not very informed when it comes to optimization but maybe add multi-core support or upgrade the unity-version. I can image that good optimization is probably a bigger step to complete but in my opinion there needs to be something done to let VRChat survive in the future.\n\nThe VRC Team already is working on a ingame event calender for the game. \nWhat will that do? \nIt will connect more and more people until all the events are filled up and only the people with the strongest PC's will \"survive\".\n\nSo please, focus on optimizing the game first VRC Team - We love your game and want to keep playing it in the future!\n\n\n- SPOONPAI",
